        "original_id": "edd0fb08-65be-5cc2-a238-60eec812207d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harry Beaumont, Theodore Wharton, Patsy Ruth Miller, Allan Forrest, Pauline Garon\n- Companies: Fox, Goldwyn, Metro, Warner Brothers, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n- Works: Rose of the World\n- Roles: film director, actor, screenwriter, producer, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Theodore Wharton (1875–1931) was an American film director, producer, and writer.\n- Harry Beaumont (February 10, 1888 – December 22, 1966) was an American film director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- In 1925, Rose of the World was released as an American silent melodrama directed by Harry Beaumont and starring Patsy Ruth Miller, Allan Forrest, and Pauline Garon.\n- Harry Beaumont worked for production companies including Fox, Goldwyn, Metro, Warner Brothers, and Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.",
